      "content": "wait, u just said the main job is to \"instill a deep, unshakeable love\" for the country? that sounds like you're saying teachers should basically ignore the heavy stuff so they don't ruin that feeling. if a kid learns about things like slavery or segregation, isn't that part of the \"truth\" they need to know? how can you say teachers shouldn't \"dwell on its sins\" when those sins are a massive part of the actual history? isn't that just teaching a version of history that's been scrubbed clean?",
